<!--
The PR title and the three sections below are published in the release notes;
everything after them is for reviewers only. The title is the headline:
`type(scope): what the user notices` in at most 72 characters, without file or
function names. `feat`, `fix`, `perf` and `revert` are shown to users; every
other type is listed under a collapsed "Internal changes".
A section that holds only a comment is skipped. Do not write "None" or "N/A":
any text you add is published.
-->

## Release note

<!-- Required for feat, perf and breaking (!) PRs, encouraged for fix; delete for other types.
One paragraph, at most 300 characters, for someone who only reads release notes:
what they can do now, or what was broken and how it showed, plus the input, flag
or step to use. No headings or lists; do not repeat the title. -->

## Usage example

<!-- Optional, feat only: one short fenced snippet users can copy. -->

## Migration

<!-- Required when the title has "!": numbered steps users must take when upgrading.
Opt-in changes that keep the current default need no migration. -->

## Description

<!-- For reviewers, never published: what changed, why, and how it was tested. -->

## Checklist

- [ ] The PR title follows [Conventional Commits](https://github.com/quokkify/ci-kit/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#branch-and-pr-title-rules) as `type(scope): summary` (scope required), with `type` one of `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `ci`, `chore`, `build`, `style`, `revert`, or `deps` (dependency updates)
- [ ] Breaking changes are marked with `!` in the title and a `## Migration` section (a `BREAKING CHANGE:` commit footer is optional)
- [ ] Tests and docs are updated
- [ ] No secrets or credentials are included
